{"name":"Blue Raspberry","hex":"#0cbfe9","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue raspberry","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A manufactured flavoring and blue food coloring for candy, snack foods, syrups, and soft drinks.","Rubus leucodermis, a species of raspberry with bluish-blackish fruit; a plant or a berry from this species."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue_raspberry"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rubus leucodermis","blocks":[{"text":"Rubus leucodermis, also called whitebark raspberry, blackcap raspberry, blue raspberry, or Chkohpeen by the Yurok is a species of Rubus native to western North America. Despite its name, it has no connection to the artificial flavoring known as blue raspberry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Rubusleucodermis.jpg/330px-Rubusleucodermis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rubus_leucodermis","wikidata":"Q1386973"},{"title":"Blue Raspberry (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Blue Raspberry is the second studio album by American singer-songwriter Katy Kirby, released on January 26, 2024. The album is Kirby's first for Anti-, explores lyrical themes of romantic exploration, and has received positive reviews from critics."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/cd/Katy_Kirby_-_Blue_Raspberry.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue_Raspberry_(album)","wikidata":"Q124342208"},{"title":"Raspberry","blocks":[{"text":"The raspberry is the edible fruit of several plant species in the genus Rubus of the rose family, most of which are in the subgenus Idaeobatus. The name also applies to these plants themselves. Raspberries are perennial with woody stems."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg/330px-Raspberry_-_halved_%28Rubus_idaeus%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raspberry","wikidata":"Q13179"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue","wikidata":"Q1088"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg/500px-Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg/960px-Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg/500px-Rubus_leucodermis_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARubus_leucodermis_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Rubus_leucodermis_4.jpg/330px-Rubus_leucodermis_4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Rubus_leucodermis_4.j